<title>BRAZIL: Brazil announces qualified B Band cellular bidders.</title>
<headline>Brazil announces qualified B Band cellular bidders.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government has announced the names of consortia that have qualified to bid on concessions to operate cellular services on the B Band frequency, an official said.</p>
<p>An official read out the names of qualified bidders for the following areas:  </p>
<p>Area Two, Sao Paulo state excluding the city of Sao Paulo -- Avantel, Brascom, TT2, Telet, BCP, GFTT and Global Telecom.</p>
<p>Area Three, Rio de Janeiro and Espirito Santo states -- Avantel, Brascom, TT2, Telet, BCP and GFTT.</p>
<p>Area Nine, Bahia and Sergipe states -- Avantel, GFTT, BSE, Americel and Vicunha.</p>
<p>The list of names for other areas were unclear. A full list of qualified bidders for the other areas was due to be distributed later Tuesday.</p>
<p>Communications Ministry press officers declined to confirm the names of qulaifiers.</p>
<p>((--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 5511 223-0358))</p>
</text>
